050551 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186083275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050551 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050551 #edb/ref 1033 727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050551 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "52c5223b-6fe6-5437-ac08-e4f0cd89565a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080087 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0bb881c0-119e-5719-8620-d731ed63efa0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080999 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6b6797a4-3539-5c2b-922f-0342c00d6829" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083042 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5879" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083042 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $2x^3+3x^2-8x-12=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "edbd084f-e8ad-53e7-9384-94094a6e7bc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083042 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-8x-12 & = \\\\ (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})-(8x+12) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(2x+3)-4(2x+3) & = \\\\ (2x+3)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(2x+3)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (2x+3)({x}^{2}-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2x+3)(x^2-4) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-2, \\; -\\dfrac{3}{2}, \\; 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083043 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083043 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $8x^3+3=4x^2+6x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90296377-6785-5b6d-87ca-8a88d4b266c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083043 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we subtract $4x^2$ and $6x$ from both sides to make the right side $0.$ To prepare for factoring by grouping, we make sure to write the resulting cubic in standard form.\n\n$$\n8x^3-4x^2-6x+3=0\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+3 & = \\\\ (8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2})-(6x-3) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{2}(2x-1)-3(2x-1) & = \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot 4{x}^{2}-(2x-1)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (2x-1)(4{x}^{2}-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve.\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(4x^2-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}, \\; \\dfrac12, \\; \\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083067 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083067 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $x^3+x^2-9x-9=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083067 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c104a42-2eea-5029-8ada-7d3bb90add52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083067 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-9x-9 & = \\\\ ({x}^{3}+{x}^{2})-(9x+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+1)-9(x+1) & = \\\\ (x+1)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(x+1)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (x+1)({x}^{2}-9) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x+1)(x^2-9) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-1, \\, \\pm  3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083068 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6111" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083068 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $-x^3-4x^2+5x+20=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083068 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d7a8d1c-449e-5e58-971f-7a063d52a703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083068 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\nx^3+4x^2-5x-20=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x-20 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+4)-5(x+4) & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-5)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x^2-5)(x+4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-4, \\pm \\sqrt 5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Cubic Equations With Leading Coefficients by Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083246 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "385b1ccd-ea68-5c59-a0e6-1a0bb7937460" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083247 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083274 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186520494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Cubic Equations With Negative Leading Coefficients by Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083275 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "01d58dfd-315a-5a4f-ae16-1db04010169a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083422 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "93504fb3-0cac-5a79-88f9-a68a78187dd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2}-6y-5=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76829beb-5936-57ec-a144-fda519a19957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083532 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2}-6y-5 & = \\\\ (12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2})-(6y+5) & = \\\\ 2{y}^{2}(6y+5)-(6y+5) & = \\\\ (6y+5)\\cdot 2{y}^{2}-(6y+5)\\cdot 1 & = \\\\ (6y+5)(2{y}^{2}-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(6y+5)(2{y}^{2}-1)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(6y+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+5 & =0 \\\\ 6y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2{y}^{2}-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37522" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $-9{y}^{3}+27{y}^{2}+y-3=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0e25d3e-3bb1-559e-a9a9-b9db2257d376" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083678 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n9{y}^{3}-27{y}^{2}-y+3=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{3}-27{y}^{2}-y+3 & = \\\\ 9{y}^{2}(y-3)-1(y-3) & = \\\\ (9{y}^{2}-1)(y-3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(9{y}^{2}-1)(y-3)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(9{y}^{2}-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(y-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084135 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084135 #edb/ref 1061 20914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084135 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "007ccdec-9f76-50fb-9833-3a3f6ac946e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084135 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084156 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084156 #edb/ref 1061 21147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084156 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f4ae760-dcdb-5fe7-ad58-6d57db23484b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084156 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084157 #edb/ref 1061 21148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084157 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "861a14bd-f811-5d0f-9526-25d3255713aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084157 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084194 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084194 #edb/ref 1061 22687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084194 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e204d6ad-cb74-5fc7-9972-8f92949eac92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084194 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084195 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084195 #edb/ref 1061 22689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084195 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6b1d8f8-0fd1-5345-a6b4-292a289f9568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084195 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084455 #edb/ref 1064 "We have learned how to solve quadratic equations by factoring. Just like quadratic equations, some (but not all) cubic equations can also be solved by factoring.\n\nTo solve a cubic equation by factoring, we just need to follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Write the equation with $0$ on one side\n\n2\\. Factor the expression on the other side\n\n3\\. Set each factor equal to $0$ and solve\n\nTo factor the cubic, we can often use the method of grouping.\n\n**Note:** The cubic equations in the following examples can all be factored, but keep in mind that most cubic equations cannot be!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084455 #edb/ref 1065 3710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084455 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3c5846e9-07ca-5d29-824a-9bb84c33473a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084455 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114145" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve ${m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "978fe695-4870-5063-84c2-77d196d63866" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233207 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6 & = \\\\ ({m}^{3}-3{m}^{2})-(2m-6) & = \\\\ {m}^{2}(m-3)-2(m-3) & = \\\\ (m-3)\\cdot {m}^{2}-(m-3)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (m-3)({m}^{2}-2) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(m-3)({m}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m-3 & =0 \\\\ m & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({m}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {m}^{2} & =2 \\\\ m & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $8{u}^{3}-6{u}^{2}-72u+54=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4ef63b9-4994-5aab-8c0b-2be94f67268a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233212 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have an overall common factor of $2$, we start by dividing our equation through by $2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27 & = \\\\ (4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2})-(36u-27) & = \\\\ {u}^{2}(4u-3)-9(4u-3) & = \\\\ (4u-3)\\cdot {u}^{2}-(4u-3)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (4u-3)({u}^{2}-9) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(4u-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-3 & =0 \\\\ 4u & =3 \\\\ u & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({u}^{2}-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2} & =9 \\\\ u & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $\\frac{3}{4}$ and $\\pm 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519998 #edb/ref 1080 "m=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519998 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519998 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0253d148-6cfe-5c62-a23b-66b9dbd84f86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520000 #edb/ref 1080 "d=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186